#: plugins/water_meter/templates/water_meter_help.html:9
msgid ""
"The plug-in measures pulses from a water meter through a PCF8583 counter at I2C address 0x50 or "
"0x51. Each uninterrupted one-second measurement produces the current flow in liters per second "
"and liters per minute."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/water_meter/templates/water_meter_help.html:10
#: plugins/wind_monitor/templates/wind_monitor_help.html:11
msgid ""
"The two I2C addresses are alternatives. If the preferred address is occupied during activation, "
"OSPy selects the free alternative. The settings page rejects an address already used by another "
"enabled plug-in, preserves the previous settings and displays the conflict in a red status bar."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/water_meter/templates/water_meter_help.html:11
msgid ""
"The overview refreshes live values every second and shows the current flow, consumption in the "
"current minute and hour, total consumption, counter state and a flow history graph."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/water_meter/templates/water_meter_help.html:12
msgid ""
"Local JSON logging and optional SQL logging can be enabled independently. The selected display "
"source supplies the measurement log, CSV download and graph. The interval is specified in "
"seconds, zero maximum records means unlimited history, and zero-flow samples can be omitted."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/water_meter/templates/water_meter_help.html:13
msgid ""
"When enabled, the Home display shows the current liters per second followed by the equivalent "
"liters per minute in parentheses and opens the Water Meter overview when selected."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/water_meter/templates/water_meter_help.html:14
msgid ""
"The mobile application receives current flow and consumption cards plus bounded flow history "
"from the selected local or SQL source."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/water_meter/templates/water_meter_help.html:15
msgid ""
"The PCF8583 count is read explicitly from registers 0x01 to 0x03. After a setup or measurement "
"failure the I2C bus is closed and initialization is retried automatically; the overview displays "
"the current I2C error instead of silently showing only zero."
